  "notes": "{閉|と}じる means to close, typically used for eyes, books, and metaphorical closings.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Can be transitive or intransitive\n- Transitive: ⟦{目|め}→目：00525_me⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{閉|と}じる (to close one's eyes)\n- Intransitive: ⟦{幕|まく}→幕：12518_maku⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{閉|と}じる (the curtain closes)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{目|め}→目：00525_me⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{閉|と}じる: to close one's eyes\n- ⟦{本|ほん}→本：00111_hon⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{閉|と}じる: to close a book\n- ⟦{口|くち}→口：00560_kuchi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{閉|と}じる: to shut one's mouth\n- ⟦{幕|まく}→幕：12518_maku⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{閉|と}じる: to bring to a close (figurative)\n- ⟦{生涯|しょうがい}→生涯：03229_shougai⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{閉|と}じる: to end one's life\n\nDISTINCTION (homophones):\n- {閉|と}じる: to close (eyes, books, figurative)\n- ⟦{綴|と}じる→綴じる：19583_tojiru⟧: to bind, staple (papers)\n\nCONTRAST WITH ⟦{閉|し}める→閉める：00485_shimeru⟧:\n{閉|と}じる is for things that open like a cover or eyelids; {閉|し}める is for doors, windows, and containers.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {閉|と}じている: is closed (resultative state)\n- Note: {閉|と}じる is a punctual verb, so {閉|と}じている describes the resulting state of being closed, not an ongoing action. ⟦{目|め}→目：00525_me⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{閉|と}じている means \"has one's eyes closed,\" not \"is in the process of closing them.\" Similarly, ⟦{本|ほん}→本：00111_hon⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{閉|と}じている means \"the book is closed.\" For the moment of closing, use {閉|と}じる or past {閉|と}じた.",
